/node_modules
node-*.tgz
# "package-lock.json" was removed here, not just at the repo root. A deeper .gitignore
# always beats a shallower re-include, so leaving this line in place would have silently
# defeated the root rule from underneath -- the root would have looked correct while this
# package's lock stayed invisible. This was the only package in the repo doing it, and it
# was found only by running "git check-ignore -v" per directory rather than trusting the
# root edit. Re-verify the same way after any change here: no output means visible.
